# Phase 4 — SSDLC

**SDLC model chosen: Iterative with continuous deployment.**

| Phase | What we did | Artefacts |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Requirements** | Interviews (informal) with 3 recent matriculants + 1 first-year student. Mapped every question learners ask post-matric. Produced a single funnel diagram. | Persona sketches, funnel diagram |
| **2. Design** | Dark-mode UI system built on design tokens. Screen inventory: 20 pages. Contract-first data shapes (course, institution, funding). | Figma-style mockups, `tokens.css`, `.js` shape definitions |
| **3. Implementation** | Built in 11 phases, each independently testable. Every phase shipped as full files (never diffs). Every phase had a verify block + test checklist before moving on. | Git history — one commit per phase |
| **4. Testing** | Manual test checklist per phase. Tested on Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Android Chrome, iOS Safari. PWA tested offline via DevTools + tunnel. | Test checklists embedded in commit messages |
| **5. Deployment** | Vercel — auto-deploys on push to `main`. Service worker precaches the app shell on first visit. In-app update prompt for every subsequent deploy. | `vercel.json`, `vite-plugin-pwa` config |
| **6. Maintenance** | No backend → no server maintenance. Data lives on the device. Updates land via the SW update prompt. | Update prompt component |

**Security considerations (documented, not hand-waved):**
- **No backend → no attack surface for server-side exploits.** Nothing leaves the device.
- **Password hashing is demo-only** — documented in `AuthContext.jsx` and README.
- **No API keys** — zero secret management overhead.
- **CSP-compatible** — no inline scripts beyond the Vite build output.
- **HTTPS required for PWA** — enforced by the browser, not by us.
- **Input validation** — every form field validated both in the UI and in `AuthContext` / `subjectRules`.

**Test coverage:**
- Every phase verified with `grep` + empty-file checks before shipping
- Browser console errors checked on every page
- PWA tested offline end-to-end
- Cross-browser verified

