# Phase 5 — Lean Business Canvas

| Block | Detail |
|---|---|
| **1. Problem** | SA matriculants don't know what they qualify for, can't afford to guess wrong, and have no single place to answer course + funding + application + rejection questions. |
| **2. Customer segments** | Primary: Grade 12 learners (matric) and their parents. Secondary: first-year tertiary students. Tertiary: schools, NGOS, government departments (DBE, DHET). |
| **3. Unique value proposition** | "Know your options. Plan your future." The only SA app that handles the *entire* post-matric journey — including what to do when you don't qualify. |
| **4. Solution** | A single installable PWA with: course matching by APS, funding discovery, application tracking, wellness, streaks, and a rule-based AI companion. |
| **5. Channels** | Word of mouth through schools · TikTok/Instagram reels for learners · WhatsApp share links · National school partnership program · DBE partnership |
| **6. Revenue streams** | Freemium: free for learners. Premium for schools (bulk accounts, dashboards). Institutional partnerships (universities pay for placement analytics). Government contracts (DBE integration). |
| **7. Cost structure** | Dev: solo-built. Hosting: free tier (Vercel, Cloudflare). Data: no servers. Marketing: organic + partnerships. Growth: content + school onboarding. |
| **8. Key metrics** | Daily active learners · Courses applied to per user · Funding save rate · Streak retention (7-day, 30-day) · Install rate · Return rate after rejection |
| **9. Unfair advantage** | The **rejection-to-recovery loop** — the only SA app that turns "you don't qualify" into a real upgrade path. Data moat: every rejection improves upgrade recommendations. |
| **10. Channels to first 1000 users** | TikTok demos · School counsellor partnerships in Gauteng · Paid micro-influencer campaign for matric season (Sep–Nov) · NSFAS deadline-aligned push |
| **11. Cost structure deep dive** | R0 infrastructure (free tier) + R0 data cost + R15–30k for initial content · R50k for first marketing burst |
| **12. Traction** | Live PWA deployed · 89 courses · 20 institutions · 24 funding options · 28 careers · 40 resources · 20 registrations in first week (internal) |

